### Auto-merge policy

`.github/workflows/auto-merge.yml` squash-merges **every** pull request whose `__HARNESS_CI_WORKFLOW__` run is green, pinned to the validated SHA, then deletes the head branch; docs-only pull requests (every file in `docs/**`, `**.md`, `LICENSE`, `.gitignore`) merge at once, without CI. **Never merged unattended**: a pull request touching Claude instruction files (`CLAUDE_GATE_RE`: `.claude/`, `CLAUDE.md`, `.githooks/`, `.mcp.json`, this workflow, the gate and its guards) or from a `claude/issue-*` head, and the Dependabot bumps the gate holds (majors, Action minors) — marked ready, merged by hand. Draft does **not** pause a pull request: cancel its CI run or close it. A merge here emits no `push` event. A workflow-touching pull request may be refused at merge while CI is green: merge it by hand, never grant `workflows: write`. → `docs/conventions/auto-merge-policy.md`
